# File discipline
- Use replace_in_file; never rewrite files over 400 lines in one shot.
- Search first, then read ±30 lines. Never whole-read large files unless small.
- Confirm edits with `git diff --stat` or `git diff <file>`.
- Pipe verification through `tail -n 40`; full logs on failure only.

# Git (phased work only)
- NEVER invoke `git commit` or `git push` directly in the terminal.
- Use `node scripts/complete-step.js <N> "<description>"` instead.
  This atomically verifies code, updates the plan checklist, commits, and pushes.

# Frontend module layout
- No build step. Plain HTML/CSS + classic JS scripts, one global scope.
- `src/app.js` is LAST and owns ONLY `window.onload` bootstrap.
- Features in `src/features/{telemetry,gear-sim,catch-log,station,auth,map}/`.
- Shared primitives in `src/shared/`.
- Target <150 lines per feature file (data/type/contract files exempt).
- Every feature file opens with `// public: a(), b() — purpose`.

# Database
- DB changes: idempotent timestamped migration under `supabase/migrations/`.
  Apply with `npx supabase db push --yes < /dev/null`.
- Verify against live DB (read-only query) before reporting done.
- `CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW` cannot rename a column: `drop view if exists` first.
- One-time data fixes are migrations too, guarded as no-ops on re-run.

# Verification
- After frontend changes: `node sanity_pass.js --quiet`.

# Memory (memory-bank/)
- New chat: read `plan.md` first. It lists all steps with [x]/[ ] status.
  Run `node scripts/plan-status.js` for a status summary.
- NEVER manually edit checkboxes (`- [ ]` / `- [x]`) in plan.md.
  The plan file is read-only during Act mode — editing is handled by
  `node scripts/complete-step.js`.
- Reference docs (`projectbrief.md`, `productContext.md`, `systemPatterns.md`,
  `techContext.md`) read only when needed.
- Do NOT read `history.md` unless explicitly asked.

# Phased workflow
- Start: read memory-bank/plan.md + run scripts/plan-status.js.
- During a step: implement code changes, but do NOT commit manually.
- Complete a step: after implementation, run:
    node scripts/complete-step.js <N> "<description>"
  This runs verification, updates plan.md, commits, pushes, and prints next step.
- If you notice an error in a previously completed step, fix the code and run:
    node scripts/complete-step.js <N> "<description>" --fix
- To check your current status or find the next task:
    node scripts/plan-status.js

# Safety
- Never run the same failing command more than twice; STOP and summarize.
- No blocking foreground servers. Background + redirect to /tmp.
- Do not write files via shell heredocs. Use the editor.